WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.375 --> 00:00:03.958
My friend John

00:00:03.958 --> 00:00:06.458
paid some pirates to go to an island

00:00:06.458 --> 00:00:08.250
to talk to people about Jesus,

00:00:09.083 --> 00:00:12.000
when he knew that he had no business doing that.

00:00:18.041 --> 00:00:20.291
John’s parents brought him up to be Christian.

00:00:21.583 --> 00:00:23.041
He was just, like, full of light.

00:00:23.625 --> 00:00:24.666
I had a little bit of a crush on him.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:27.000
You couldn't have asked for a better
young man.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.041
He reminds me of who
I wanted to serve with.

00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:33.291
He told me his plan was to go
live in the middle of the jungle.

00:00:34.208 --> 00:00:35.791
It didn't sound that bad.

00:00:36.708 --> 00:00:40.541
I thought that John would get accepted.

00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:45.336
People whose language
no one speaks,

00:00:45.336 --> 00:00:47.588
whose culture no one knows.

00:00:50.291 --> 00:00:52.666
There's a fine line
between faith and madness.

00:00:54.458 --> 00:00:56.625
Once he found out about that tribe,

00:00:56.625 --> 00:00:58.916
he knew he was going to go all in.

00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:01.250
John was telling a story,

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:02.666
“I'm a climber. I'm an adventurer.”

00:01:02.666 --> 00:01:03.791
Here we are, hiking out!

00:01:03.791 --> 00:01:04.875
If things don't go well.

00:01:04.916 --> 00:01:08.234
He wanted to look like a young, arrogant,
western person

00:01:08.818 --> 00:01:11.362
did a stupid thing and move on.

00:01:12.916 --> 00:01:15.250
John said to me,
“This is what the plan looks like.”

00:01:15.458 --> 00:01:16.375
“Have it right here.”

00:01:17.916 --> 00:01:21.708
There are so many ways
the seductions of this story can go wrong.

00:01:21.958 --> 00:01:25.293
This idea of people who exist out of time,

00:01:25.876 --> 00:01:27.462
 that erases their humanity.

00:01:27.625 --> 00:01:29.333
These cultures that are isolated,

00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:33.750
when we cross that boundary,
we're saying, “Your prohibition means nothing to us.”

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:35.875
That there's a group that we would decide

00:01:35.875 --> 00:01:38.166
“Sorry, you don't get to hear about Jesus,”

00:01:38.166 --> 00:01:40.250
that's a violation of their human right.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.250
John did exactly
what Jesus told him to do.

00:01:42.625 --> 00:01:45.541
John was pursuing a fantasy.

00:01:46.666 --> 00:01:49.666
In discerning the call,

00:01:49.666 --> 00:01:50.958
we can mess it up.

00:01:52.208 --> 00:01:55.916
My friend
did something stupid and courageous

00:01:55.916 --> 00:01:59.000
and bold, and I wish I was that bold.

